  "finalReply": "Created `/app/program.py`, a byte-exact Python re-implementation of `src/program.cbl`.\n\nKey behaviors replicated from GnuCOBOL 3 probing (compile/run/diff):\n- Fixed-length record-sequential I/O with no delimiters: ACCOUNTS 34B, BOOKS 28B, TRANSACTIONS/INPUT 22B; short INPUT padded with spaces, long INPUT (trailing newline/extra records) truncated to first 22B; empty INPUT prints `Error: Input file is empty` with no changes.\n- Numeric DISPLAY: spaces/non-digits act as zeros (`\"200\"+7 spaces → 2000000000`); balances/amounts zero-padded to 10 digits.\n- Unsigned arithmetic: buyer debit stores negative results as absolute value; seller credit wraps modulo 10¹⁰.\n- Validation (exact 4B ID/owner compares) prints `\" \"` then success/fail messages; failed validation leaves all files untouched.\n- `buyer == seller` with passing validation reproduces the COBOL crash: only the first matching account is debited, books/transactions untouched, no success message.\n- `OPEN EXTEND` on missing `TRANSACTIONS.DAT` updates accounts/books but creates nothing.\n\nVerified with 24 differential scenarios (valid/short/space/zero/overflow/negative amounts, invalid buyer/seller/book/owner, empty files, missing transaction file, multi-record input, duplicate IDs, buyer==seller) — all `.DAT` outputs identical between COBOL and Python, and original `/app/data/*` + `/app/src/INPUT.DAT` state restored.",
